    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i just can't stop thinking about it. that kid in the hallway, months ago... i just stood there. i watched them get cornered and i did nothing. i even felt this weird sense of relief that it wasn't me. i feel like there's just something fundamentally broken in my core. like i'm just a bad person masquerading as a human.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is very frightening to feel that you've failed someone, but remember that humans are not defined by their worst moments, especially those born from fear or a desire to stay safe. Many people struggle with similar intrusive thoughts and second-guessing long after the event, which doesn't necessarily mean they are \"bad.\" Instead of labeling yourself harshly, consider speaking with a counselor who can help you process these emotions without judgment. Healing this shame is entirely possible, and you deserve to feel at peace with who you are right now.",
